   "answer": "When the Manager moved us to the front window, I was careful not to look too eager. Rosa said the Sun would notice us sooner there, but I wasn't sure it worked that way. “Be patient,” the Manager told us. “The right child will come.”\n\nI watched the taxis stop and start—yellow, then grey, then yellow again—and tried to remember every face that paused at the glass. Some looked for a long time; others hardly looked at all. I didn't yet understand why a person would walk past so quickly, as though the window were only a reflection of the street.",
